Alembic migrations for UyHub.

The database URL comes from DATABASE_URL via uyhub.core.config, never from
alembic.ini — migrations and the application therefore always target the same
database.

Usage (from the repository root):

    make migrate                      apply everything   -> alembic upgrade head
    make migration m="add listings"   new revision       -> alembic revision --autogenerate

Rules (CLAUDE.md "Code rules"):

  * Schema changes happen only through a new revision.
  * Never edit a revision that has been applied anywhere. Write a new one.
  * Every revision must have a working downgrade; `make test` asserts that
    upgrade -> downgrade -> upgrade is clean.
  * Review autogenerated revisions by hand. Autogenerate does not detect renames
    (it emits drop + add, which loses data) and it does not order index creation
    for large tables.

Revision 0001 is an intentionally empty baseline; it only enables pg_trgm.
